      "writtenOn": "2026-09-29T16:30:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do the same for other cache keys [CachedAccountDetails](https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/heads/master/java/com/google/gerrit/server/account/CachedAccountDetails.java#42) or [ConflictKey](https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/heads/master/java/com/google/gerrit/server/query/change/ConflictKey.java#34)\n\nI believe the intention is to ensure that the object inserted in the key cannot be mutated later. Otherwise, the cache may no longer find its entry.\n\nThe `copy()` documentation states:\n\n```\n...\nThis method is useful to shed any additional memory that may be tied to the\n subclass, yet retain the unique identity of the object id for future lookups \n within maps and repositories.\n...\n```\n\nWDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "35e565bb_f5d170bd",
      "revId": "f2f8c01e21ad6f5375ac2e19c80c22441fbde7da",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
