      "writtenOn": "2026-09-29T16:30:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could add a method receiving the revision to\nDirectAuthTokenAccessor and have the loader delegate to it.\n\nThe loader already opens `All-Users` because it needs to load exactly the revision in the cache key. \n\nMoving it to `DirectAuthTokenAccessor` would either require passing the open Repository to a new internal method, or make the accessor open it itself, if I understand what you meant.\n\nThis follows the same pattern as `AccountCacheImpl`\u0027s loader, which opens the\nrepository and loads the revision from its cache key directly.\n\nI think keeping it here is a little simpler and avoids expanding DirectAuthTokenAccessor for this cache-only use case, but please correct me if I have the wrong side of the stick here.",
